#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b92d5a-d1df-55d9-b76c-8340b0cdd31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235801} {:answer/id #uuid "17fbd976-22a0-5f3c-a91e-40fd34a09bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235964} {:answer/id #uuid "8e805a00-40af-55fc-a317-73b147f7007a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236720} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc2f2ab-bdce-542e-b352-c5b04b7f8a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236815} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fd5bc7-78fe-503f-ab40-8f0d8119f8a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17fbd976-22a0-5f3c-a91e-40fd34a09bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235964} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e7f2652-5876-52bb-86dd-90e0f34762b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd551375-bd59-5d04-876f-c42f8931f73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102687" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡t & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t & =\\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡t}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{x}.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d5e141-e738-5b2a-a703-6da0a982dde0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236350} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8ce46e-daf7-55c0-89df-337038a09ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236422} {:answer/id #uuid "68ed4719-9dea-5337-9667-8f3e5657f5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236480} {:answer/id #uuid "7f133e8a-78f1-5235-b7a3-a3e3ba78ba25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236604} {:answer/id #uuid "d944ae68-297d-5663-a79f-21d577d3bda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53d5e141-e738-5b2a-a703-6da0a982dde0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236350} :answer-field/id #uuid "33a55434-2f0c-5beb-95aa-d1250e59d512" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "962d8665-19cf-5669-bc0c-46b711cf96ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-102922" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,y={sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0854b8df-7a7a-57f6-b376-2a218e36ff2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235854} {:answer/id #uuid "6acdc17f-072f-5f68-86af-7572c7fd6f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236490} {:answer/id #uuid "8afcd281-1318-594a-a9ba-52f65fa8ef56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236686} {:answer/id #uuid "bf44f6a5-6c3e-5582-ba6b-2ec5a73ba371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237032} {:answer/id #uuid "e72bd93b-5cde-5f30-8245-c6eb24cfb3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf44f6a5-6c3e-5582-ba6b-2ec5a73ba371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237032} :answer-field/id #uuid "067447ca-a94b-5969-ab12-e75c926f9806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f469ae9f-d511-5b2e-b179-c38dadb0919b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102940" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}+3,\\,y=3{t}^{5}+{t}^{3},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4t}=\\frac{3t(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(1)(5(1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12419a49-8a72-5d5a-b25b-542fc5dab0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235925} {:answer/id #uuid "4a01b9e0-c4f0-5704-a712-09144764bfa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236292} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2e0013-e151-51e9-ad4a-bbb0f6be0b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237009} {:answer/id #uuid "c954ba9f-6430-5221-9f47-5bf333b81728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237094} {:answer/id #uuid "f813ee90-74dd-524e-9db4-b206cc8dc2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12419a49-8a72-5d5a-b25b-542fc5dab0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235925} :answer-field/id #uuid "74a48016-4413-5cfa-822b-c23d4158c7f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7720b821-7c21-51f2-9679-46c0e6df53a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102941" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{4}{\\pi }{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{8}{\\pi }t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{\\pi }t)}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2})}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "384052f7-8479-5451-8826-ebad4be0b9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236174} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ceb671-4df1-5711-99a6-e539d10040f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237068} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf06b23-9d73-58e3-96a2-bad6a11980c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237111} {:answer/id #uuid "d5aad3f9-96d0-5577-81a4-3ff8e34b23b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237166} {:answer/id #uuid "fd975286-7f8a-5f9b-80aa-d25b3f4ae72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5ceb671-4df1-5711-99a6-e539d10040f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237068} :answer-field/id #uuid "3adb5c55-83aa-583d-aebb-812163c6902d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1839cab9-bd67-5688-9a2a-104436b124ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-103540" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c05b61-7dc6-53f0-8eed-7743ecb92787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235813} {:answer/id #uuid "837899b1-cc2e-59cf-a23a-35f2ed00b6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236639} {:answer/id #uuid "90b48184-136a-57ff-a6c6-8aa6ad551689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236738} {:answer/id #uuid "9673d4c2-53f4-5a56-9462-97e02a7c3a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236772} {:answer/id #uuid "b4be8d8f-4a66-536f-b059-008317284b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "837899b1-cc2e-59cf-a23a-35f2ed00b6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236639} :answer-field/id #uuid "452b7748-b2b6-53f6-b879-d5ef2699fbff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a06523df-238f-57e5-936a-f93168e3e76d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103541" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-3,2,0⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-4,2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{77}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2x\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2x\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(4x-0)i-(-6x-0)j+(12-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,6x,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52{x}^{2}+64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{77} \\\\ \\sqrt{52{x}^{2}+64} & =\\sqrt{77} \\\\ 52{x}^{2}+64 & =77 \\\\ 52{x}^{2} & =13 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1042b2b0-48dd-582d-b30e-d64f5e68e655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235904} {:answer/id #uuid "531f08ba-c26d-5ffb-b31b-76da888b8b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236345} {:answer/id #uuid "95806bed-6677-52d1-86f0-a9c3b398a75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236766} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc5b9af-1b07-5068-bffd-2500e6a28cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237209} {:answer/id #uuid "eb84ec79-c885-5346-994b-a3ef1e3618cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1042b2b0-48dd-582d-b30e-d64f5e68e655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235904} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd051b8-cfd0-500d-b748-e9e245e480d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e8a01d-ba49-5e10-81ec-e89893b65589" :question/math-academy-id "q-103542" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2396dede-1b82-5a2a-aa5a-3223ea475b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236045} {:answer/id #uuid "5d433363-5f65-5914-a92b-e08e2d8de45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236404} {:answer/id #uuid "acd9a719-7f3e-5a4e-b249-7cef823b6db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236917} {:answer/id #uuid "b8694282-defb-545d-a22d-31c29f015388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236996} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4c7f2d-5e99-56fc-9df8-7f1922ff63db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d433363-5f65-5914-a92b-e08e2d8de45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236404} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1bd1fc-a71d-5a23-a644-e9a570aa5b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc2ecbe1-ea04-53ab-bfa6-277a8ca05a39" :question/math-academy-id "q-103547" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨4,x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,3,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{181}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & x & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}4 & x \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0-9)i-(0+6)j+(12+2x)k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-6,12+2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(12+2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+36+144+48x+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ \\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ 261+48x+4{x}^{2} & =181 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+48x+80 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x+20 & =0 \\\\ (x+10)(x+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-10,\\,-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc2a099-bf95-50e1-b9c3-7330e50dafc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236020} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7bbb8f-90eb-5b64-af7c-61e67a66ae8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236104} {:answer/id #uuid "422c528b-268c-59a9-aa08-17ee3b5fb935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236239} {:answer/id #uuid "457328c4-1a16-5b0d-8e61-d406b9702bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236264} {:answer/id #uuid "a01206ba-e5ec-539f-b8df-b8f8806d9468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422c528b-268c-59a9-aa08-17ee3b5fb935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236239} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b389ae5-8e6c-5abf-8392-283e3441d1c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e02b899-797e-55fb-bf98-84a59903fc4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103549" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,3,4⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,-x,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{221}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -x & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(6+4x)i-(0+4)j+(0+3)k \\\\  & =⟨6+4x,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(6+4x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+48x+16{x}^{2}+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61+48x+16{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{221} \\\\ \\sqrt{61+48x+16{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{221} \\\\ 61+48x+16{x}^{2} & =221 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}+48x-160 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3x-10 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)(x-2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-5,\\,2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139a429e-ade1-501e-b65f-dac725fd7e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235932} {:answer/id #uuid "16719391-8dec-5e82-b401-93ca0e8487a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235956} {:answer/id #uuid "49cb3763-a9d5-5bb5-9b6a-9d363519fada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236290} {:answer/id #uuid "a927a9d7-e41d-58d1-9c3c-54f2ab45e590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236882} {:answer/id #uuid "aa115508-6b4c-591b-b7d1-64700634a6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a927a9d7-e41d-58d1-9c3c-54f2ab45e590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236882} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde4e8a4-64c8-57b9-ac27-5d4fb7853626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "357e8faf-9623-5ade-84da-303c65f27082" :question/math-academy-id "q-103552" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,1,-2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{53}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2x\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2x\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(4x-3)i-(0+6)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x-3,-6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+9+36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61} & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+61 & =53 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (2x-1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c79e65f-4657-574d-9b28-b9892ee40b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i-y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238293} {:answer/id #uuid "7eceeb7e-4643-589d-8a42-a35eb4275ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i+y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239158} {:answer/id #uuid "8baa56bb-b0ab-5fd3-9d83-4ae38a0f0cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239266} {:answer/id #uuid "a8db757c-0e28-5da6-9dc7-d0eddb5e601d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239527} {:answer/id #uuid "c5cda0b4-4f82-58cb-b44a-ebd0359b68ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5cda0b4-4f82-58cb-b44a-ebd0359b68ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239796} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0577431-9e1f-5827-b110-3279dc00b9e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f3ac565-e5b1-59a8-9f54-0c7e96f05c2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104396" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i-j \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=2x\\,i-j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45db7d37-257e-5741-9767-a2ee72bc303f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+2y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238662} {:answer/id #uuid "a026c4f1-65e8-584a-81f8-49d09aed3845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239453} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b3803d-0406-5f4c-b4f7-02086d600d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239500} {:answer/id #uuid "b49e4fa1-e304-508a-b582-63a15e87c038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239636} {:answer/id #uuid "c17f4964-aa3f-54ce-b990-6a3cc4bcb36c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{2y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6b3803d-0406-5f4c-b4f7-02086d600d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239500} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dcac30f-063e-5f3e-b8eb-a855b3db8035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "139d3292-e475-5138-868b-b4cb7235237f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104397" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})j \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271a1e1f-1ff6-50b3-b5d4-c1267966fd1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238393} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf4b57e-a5d8-5197-87f7-4d37497177cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238584} {:answer/id #uuid "4fcb3d5f-1df2-530a-a137-6eb6c29edfb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238741} {:answer/id #uuid "602128e3-6a58-54b5-9c00-03a9dc5cebe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238897} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfb84d9-8417-5a4e-acd5-04777c4b55e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddfb84d9-8417-5a4e-acd5-04777c4b55e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239992} :answer-field/id #uuid "95d8cc0b-f8f2-5892-9930-6c06feb6852d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbb95ba6-f378-5cdd-befa-8f5b533b38d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-104398" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y)$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3y))\\,j \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-3y)\\,j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e828d95-ecbc-57d8-b8d9-acf763b088e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238462} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6e3eea-6dbc-567a-b7c6-ba10a5fed190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238572} {:answer/id #uuid "541fb43b-1bee-5827-afeb-bd3595f7ffbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238779} {:answer/id #uuid "7802141d-b50b-5e83-be03-15a439e33fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239092} {:answer/id #uuid "a8355852-7497-53ad-930e-a02821cc5439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7802141d-b50b-5e83-be03-15a439e33fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239092} :answer-field/id #uuid "816ba5d9-4c22-58e9-ba7c-700eb48c8a5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f05e7a0d-26f2-588a-8d78-a6a57d732300" :question/math-academy-id "q-104410" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=(ay-2x{y}^{3})\\,i+(x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,j$ on ${R}^{2},$ where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ we have $P=ay-2x{y}^{3}$ and $Q=x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=a-6x{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-6x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-6x{y}^{2} & =1-6x{y}^{2} \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1bc900-62d1-5615-af0f-6dbe4ee35a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238300} {:answer/id #uuid "2899ff60-966e-5c9f-a77b-cd076462b487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238412} {:answer/id #uuid "501fc527-192e-54f2-86ab-52b7b2842115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238747} {:answer/id #uuid "dac6fd53-9350-56e6-9302-b6846604e6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239963} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b1e404-5480-5ec1-86f2-cbf9a0ee1d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2899ff60-966e-5c9f-a77b-cd076462b487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238412} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74e5e09-607e-5411-a367-f75da43c0068" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bd6d6aa-1b16-5a93-a052-cdf54093004e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104414" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\frac{axy}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,j$ on ${R}^{2},$ where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ we have $P=\\frac{axy}{{x}^{2}+1}$ and $Q=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{ax}{{x}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{ax}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ ax & =2x \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5650cae6-4ebd-5fab-b924-a7307b4e29a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437372} {:answer/id #uuid "6993da07-2440-58cb-93b7-f9bd99118665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6993da07-2440-58cb-93b7-f9bd99118665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437373} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e37b67f-127d-5c2b-b4d2-843eb6fcfe09" :answer-field/key "$F=(2x-y)\\,i-x\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46b38472-837a-578d-bc86-3da38e6632e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437374} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3efb19-98f5-5322-9115-86ca840350d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3efb19-98f5-5322-9115-86ca840350d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437375} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18ab833-d485-51f2-bc95-50bb5a8ff3bb" :answer-field/key "$G=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5941ba21-ceee-5f9b-91b5-ac8cf172b28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437376} {:answer/id #uuid "15d3424b-50ff-5a9b-a7ba-8a86b14dd910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d3424b-50ff-5a9b-a7ba-8a86b14dd910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437377} :answer-field/id #uuid "6df86221-3e95-5646-bb83-ccb26044056c" :answer-field/key "$H={e}^{x-y}\\,i-{e}^{x-y}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff94cca-f0c0-5b4f-9e96-5ccdc57e1837" :question/math-academy-id "q-104573" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields. \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=2x-y$ and $Q=-x.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ and $Q=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={e}^{x-y}$ and $Q=-{e}^{x-y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{x-y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{e}^{x-y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F=(2x-y)\\,i-x\\,j$; $G=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j$; $H={e}^{x-y}\\,i-{e}^{x-y}\\,j$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65481b7b-861e-5720-a6dd-8d674d4da852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437384} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2c88c4-d301-5e5f-ada9-7861ac00371d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65481b7b-861e-5720-a6dd-8d674d4da852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437384} :answer-field/id #uuid "20435457-d381-5fe1-8f30-f9db1f097122" :answer-field/key "$F=(2x-4y)\\,i+(4x-8y)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "721521bd-d66b-56ad-b5bc-1f9a532924dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437386} {:answer/id #uuid "3b297167-e02b-58b6-a123-5866263ab82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b297167-e02b-58b6-a123-5866263ab82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437387} :answer-field/id #uuid "28606333-ca6f-5543-bf82-4a014fa763e8" :answer-field/key "$G={2}^{2x+y+1}\\,i+{2}^{2x+y}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a53745e3-b275-5699-876b-c7e875b44edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437388} {:answer/id #uuid "53a6adf6-bbaa-5c44-b75e-33daf101bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53a6adf6-bbaa-5c44-b75e-33daf101bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437389} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd839e2a-5adc-5c75-b668-ba299a877b00" :answer-field/key "$H=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aac0da30-e1e4-5293-838c-ddb161ffe326" :question/math-academy-id "q-104582" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative in their respective domains?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.\n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=2x-4y$ and $Q=4x-8y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $F$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P={2}^{2x+y+1}$ and $Q={2}^{2x+y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)$ and $Q=\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $G={2}^{2x+y+1}\\,i+{2}^{2x+y}\\,j$; $H=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,j$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240974 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb2fea76-d8f1-5666-a542-917bd5baee71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437390} {:answer/id #uuid "152c789f-5317-52e2-9188-28255c154716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "152c789f-5317-52e2-9188-28255c154716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437391} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ac27b51-3d78-5bc3-a8f8-810b27ff1b38" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a9ffcb-44f2-5949-95fa-814bfb8cc5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437392} {:answer/id #uuid "2efd0294-1666-5152-a16a-9dd09a7d9ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3a9ffcb-44f2-5949-95fa-814bfb8cc5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437392} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9e6c62-67a6-523e-b1cd-fd7207ec866b" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8adb53a3-b021-5071-855f-0576c8b568b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437394} {:answer/id #uuid "7405feb1-7683-5595-b311-1a84859ab6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8adb53a3-b021-5071-855f-0576c8b568b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437394} :answer-field/id #uuid "925b2332-69df-5291-870e-c0a3f090f25c" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7bfa530-747d-5ad6-84ad-036bd0059f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437396} {:answer/id #uuid "77ab6b50-7aec-5c00-9718-d684cc7f9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ab6b50-7aec-5c00-9718-d684cc7f9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437397} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f99b753-4981-57eb-8141-5cc7a73668b9" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b5e7ba9-0b08-5996-9edf-60b5549da2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-105046" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bc0e75bb577ca37b89568e14a4e0d03da7ce4f4853c4e8c57d9b2df79897b13.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F=0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F>0$ and $∇\\cdot F<0$ are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F=0$; “$F$ is solenoidal” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b0b80fa-496f-569a-9899-ee3fbf9e50a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238702} {:answer/id #uuid "82fba072-abfd-5d9f-a6f8-d005dbba793d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239196} {:answer/id #uuid "a289a29e-002e-5ce1-832a-10dd82584b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+2x{cos}^{2}⁡y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239467} {:answer/id #uuid "b33afbcd-dddc-52bd-b80a-39711f698a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239618} {:answer/id #uuid "b3995c52-98a6-533d-a3a3-c2e12da1579b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x{cos}^{2}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b33afbcd-dddc-52bd-b80a-39711f698a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239618} :answer-field/id #uuid "76e1c659-7566-5775-b915-e264f8844bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ed9b106-fbec-5b47-bde6-fc871e3c0688" :question/math-academy-id "q-105554" :question/problem "Given that $F=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+{x}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡y\\,j,$ what is $\\text{div}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡y) \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc992ec-1afd-513d-b4a8-935bf11a1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437414} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ae86bd-dc3b-5370-ab3b-9336719bd2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc992ec-1afd-513d-b4a8-935bf11a1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437414} :answer-field/id #uuid "edadb83c-1055-5eb5-a587-5d624186af4e" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d980f6-7dd1-52ed-9c35-3b5cd4be9f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437416} {:answer/id #uuid "956ccca4-670f-5c14-940c-9c94b57e93ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "956ccca4-670f-5c14-940c-9c94b57e93ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437417} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f0a995-38e4-5d57-8347-383ed693a19a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438737} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfcaf0b4-948d-526a-b01f-36bdeaf81642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437418} {:answer/id #uuid "cd95d5af-5c40-5c79-8812-a19589b0d35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfcaf0b4-948d-526a-b01f-36bdeaf81642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437418} :answer-field/id #uuid "832e5215-2f00-59ba-acd0-9dda792a61d4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3bd3a4-af83-5047-8b63-efebd317e224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437420} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f48472-2cb4-54b3-9e60-7c12a6e8a9b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3bd3a4-af83-5047-8b63-efebd317e224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437420} :answer-field/id #uuid "98632cbf-edce-5596-bc40-b3809453d48c" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c30bad2f-8979-5b57-acae-23ae1c82d606" :question/math-academy-id "q-105573" :question/problem "![](images/30/3088d088689bbd0dfd33abe8240c6f02cceb257937fc1fccb8ba3df151dbfaab.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3758688-c398-5563-9ef4-6725bb756a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437422} {:answer/id #uuid "20c2906c-786b-5d44-a2ab-80b29dc77300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c2906c-786b-5d44-a2ab-80b29dc77300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437423} :answer-field/id #uuid "19f46c09-a764-5deb-8de8-68af7432ea43" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc20a89d-06eb-52ee-876e-878056126986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437424} {:answer/id #uuid "af5eb708-473f-56c4-b243-76dd14db4f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc20a89d-06eb-52ee-876e-878056126986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437424} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a39fa9-d231-5fb4-8edd-c467842038cf" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15199d6a-677b-53ea-8492-a7aa4a7eb581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437426} {:answer/id #uuid "19d090b2-e9f5-5f83-9d51-046d10ff6235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15199d6a-677b-53ea-8492-a7aa4a7eb581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437426} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5999586-c6a2-5268-a3ec-230c0f2be240" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4882a295-c5c0-51e1-926e-f95e716e654e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437428} {:answer/id #uuid "9067697b-3c5f-57eb-bc0d-1edcb637afcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9067697b-3c5f-57eb-bc0d-1edcb637afcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437429} :answer-field/id #uuid "564a4db5-ce17-5a9f-8f0c-cf41329af0c2" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2172851-a396-51c3-bd4e-4e1278b37143" :question/math-academy-id "q-105575" :question/problem "![](images/11/11d38951b884f17616a61403d793322d0e2ea28910e806fe8f018251508352a1.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F=0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F>0$ and $∇\\cdot F<0$ are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F=0$; “$F$ is solenoidal” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b18a510-e720-57fd-926f-ab9d3c48a75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437430} {:answer/id #uuid "72d86651-4a74-5ff6-9fd1-824929e1123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72d86651-4a74-5ff6-9fd1-824929e1123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437431} :answer-field/id #uuid "665fa786-ea66-5817-b113-1425709d275c" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "571970a0-5082-56bc-8c15-26d049fea5cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437432} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e78f39-2b47-52f9-9502-52e150a46b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "571970a0-5082-56bc-8c15-26d049fea5cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437432} :answer-field/id #uuid "3664e7f0-c10a-541a-a220-0f4c16709dde" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf4e34d1-780b-506e-9e3c-cafa56bb51ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437434} {:answer/id #uuid "d1badd00-e59a-5384-b8e9-55b06e178011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf4e34d1-780b-506e-9e3c-cafa56bb51ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437434} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b68b5d7-cbb4-57e0-97c5-32750d8465c8" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e9fc12-438f-5541-b60c-9f5f8f8d604a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437436} {:answer/id #uuid "b331f531-ebb7-5ebc-9843-2ad0f3951cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b331f531-ebb7-5ebc-9843-2ad0f3951cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437437} :answer-field/id #uuid "4361eabc-2c9b-5d9c-b0eb-aca3674799ba" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02256216-cf21-5a66-b1b3-c31d4444cdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-105576" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf932f4f02a216d5111da0748cb04f815a7d2e85af5db2f9282f5aefc359b816.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F=0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F>0$ and $∇\\cdot F<0$ are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F=0$; “$F$ is solenoidal” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4bb96b-8edc-5609-ae5d-59c93968d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437446} {:answer/id #uuid "214ccabe-bb6d-5e3e-82a7-5b85941906ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b4bb96b-8edc-5609-ae5d-59c93968d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437446} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9bde054-a083-5ff8-8b6a-04f7bc56d333" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17375072-dff9-5140-a8fd-b8472c42ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437448} {:answer/id #uuid "a81f8472-e1f1-5068-a130-52aada50a600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81f8472-e1f1-5068-a130-52aada50a600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437449} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e24b59-c778-516f-80a2-667e53327c27" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438753} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a898aa-548e-5265-9ae2-a3dafc762fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437450} {:answer/id #uuid "572c91ee-3d7b-56b5-a52b-d18d82413c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6a898aa-548e-5265-9ae2-a3dafc762fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437450} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f846d1-462e-5476-ad72-5ffdce32e670" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438754} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db9829d-7585-53f2-9f60-fe945a3c2914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437452} {:answer/id #uuid "cc11d7ed-75ec-5de5-94fc-3d0209cb4b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9db9829d-7585-53f2-9f60-fe945a3c2914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437452} :answer-field/id #uuid "e218f141-6fbf-52b2-a3d6-8f410c56d947" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2be15a89-9d36-55d5-9fa3-9993a8ff3b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105578" :question/problem "![](images/33/33f0353e3856fb2b458d17ed1959918e6a3dd96fd0a966d971575ffc212402f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move horizontally and vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dec2cc2-3405-52c3-8979-abd8eb2a2b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437462} {:answer/id #uuid "0794f2ce-66e5-5eee-bc4d-0db5a27294c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0794f2ce-66e5-5eee-bc4d-0db5a27294c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437463} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b78da69-9857-55b5-bd09-bf9713a7e40e" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66323cd6-6318-59a5-8c75-296ec59e3c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437464} {:answer/id #uuid "421e51c5-959b-56e2-af2c-c59025f76191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66323cd6-6318-59a5-8c75-296ec59e3c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437464} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5add59-bb91-5d45-ba13-41f76566398c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7c0fd7b-0c6b-5e56-bd17-a792412d0f1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437466} {:answer/id #uuid "78ef5d9e-ab86-5f26-8bdf-f69df52aee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78ef5d9e-ab86-5f26-8bdf-f69df52aee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437467} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff65ca0f-7924-5e1e-b45b-e82396f639fd" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c3454f9-4f94-5d9c-9504-95bd742d6fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437468} {:answer/id #uuid "a286c0c8-6b91-5628-897c-39200ea30c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c3454f9-4f94-5d9c-9504-95bd742d6fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437468} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa53b8b-f892-5eaf-a4df-840413a09c4a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7d9f8f8-5aac-59da-a7d3-267484c84687" :question/math-academy-id "q-105667" :question/problem "![](images/77/773ff9d880deed92f8034d6949cfee85edbcdf735c8e125f1ec5762137fadb9c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/4e/4e344a0a1f6b0c535c5ba08ee8c87914cf5e7009600f45732023720048b4c493.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements “$F$ is irrotational” is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statements “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$; “$F$ is irrotational” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1639f667-cc0c-541f-beb3-df7075bcd242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238243} {:answer/id #uuid "746766cf-a9af-578f-8dc5-0e36b21b4e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239054} {:answer/id #uuid "7681ef8d-3f67-572c-af5f-8f55918debf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239078} {:answer/id #uuid "7de0f017-aa4f-55fa-b7f6-e4e3b289359f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239147} {:answer/id #uuid "e7823a5e-3336-5cc7-868c-2023128957eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6z\\,j+2\\,\\text{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7de0f017-aa4f-55fa-b7f6-e4e3b289359f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239147} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2209b7-9fdc-539d-9358-25e617c5c773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b3b1abb-e804-5079-8fb6-32a843b8454e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105668" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=3{z}^{2}\\,i+2y\\,j+k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & 2y & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-6z)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =6z\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437470} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaad2e3-2efd-5e19-bb7f-b57ea3fc6e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437470} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c08d5d7-5b76-5798-9849-c11e4265495c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af0ccef4-0d9f-5258-a00a-2d3b70919956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437472} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f2d444-ce1a-575d-8dd5-cb8eca23b4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f2d444-ce1a-575d-8dd5-cb8eca23b4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437473} :answer-field/id #uuid "05bb4ba6-a345-5135-97e0-a2bde6d14a93" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f909166-7a9f-5343-b5ec-b4d1d3560f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437474} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3f9244-257c-5be9-95ea-d30230d49bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e3f9244-257c-5be9-95ea-d30230d49bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437475} :answer-field/id #uuid "690da8d3-c31e-5a96-8f2e-4923d49f0a94" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1438c53-192f-52c6-a875-55bb696d0ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437476} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2db5d5-ff4e-5705-a9a3-8abc334919c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1438c53-192f-52c6-a875-55bb696d0ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437476} :answer-field/id #uuid "91d192c0-fb0c-5d05-a1b4-1e76869a1358" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c2154fc-c947-5ba9-b169-f98f4fea25a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105669" :question/problem "![](images/24/2414de6e2129d4fceaae304d16f9be0c91a545e5a8544b2033f353ddb2e581b9.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecf86ba1-b225-5f4e-a85f-182bd2bdbc53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437478} {:answer/id #uuid "c7744411-0aa5-54ef-9c74-d6ca7e53bdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7744411-0aa5-54ef-9c74-d6ca7e53bdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437479} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1fc1b7-1f6d-5789-bbaf-748a9803bc96" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9168e608-76cb-5350-991f-3427546bf922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437480} {:answer/id #uuid "6acf104d-e9d0-56e0-a85c-9b1ece39cee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9168e608-76cb-5350-991f-3427546bf922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437480} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aa0313b-ee82-5436-b649-0b4504bba2d2" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf15f6c8-cfc5-5bbe-886a-d7a4c35fe3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437482} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab85c7d-e507-5369-a231-49fca8b2c436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ab85c7d-e507-5369-a231-49fca8b2c436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437483} :answer-field/id #uuid "c223aec0-697d-56a5-825e-44718ec7f2d3" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d8d559-74b6-5016-bfae-9833564ce138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437484} {:answer/id #uuid "ee14db71-cbc6-5c05-87b0-f9afe0453fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d8d559-74b6-5016-bfae-9833564ce138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437484} :answer-field/id #uuid "28f80fe3-8688-556e-8b02-a42b1e403d0f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54529993-0bd1-511f-b362-f0eafc672ef8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105671" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c38294780ac6d5079b759f39a7dbd4944b1c3c21495245dfd314ec180c0434e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/97/979b63f21e56924bd7880f9487cf829089e38cf14d287e70196c7a661e41f97f.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$; “$F$ is irrotational” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133c1b20-5150-50da-8523-674470a0cfe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238215} {:answer/id #uuid "5c8be352-8015-5be2-b8df-9a4f3ad0aa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238865} {:answer/id #uuid "82de7a70-0733-5cde-9eac-f208a1690d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239194} {:answer/id #uuid "82fbfc1b-0c81-5da1-927a-375691efc6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239197} {:answer/id #uuid "853fbdfa-bdb1-5373-adfe-5cf0720fa54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82fbfc1b-0c81-5da1-927a-375691efc6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239197} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42bc9e6-d9aa-54be-b2ee-e7d0d024b8b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8f1a0a3-0b71-52cd-b327-6c0ec92e34be" :question/math-academy-id "q-105672" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={e}^{y+z}\\,i+j+xyz\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{y+z} & 1 & xyz\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y+z})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y+z})]k \\\\  & =(xz-0)i-(yz-{e}^{y+z})j+(0-{e}^{y+z})k \\\\  & =xz\\,i+({e}^{y+z}-yz)j-{e}^{y+z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,1,-1) & =2(-1)\\,i+({e}^{1+(-1)}-1(-1))j-{e}^{1+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6da5be-dab7-5557-9faa-e9c458176103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437486} {:answer/id #uuid "c92cf9d4-7709-5ceb-b895-b546ae07415c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d6da5be-dab7-5557-9faa-e9c458176103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437486} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e9da93-54af-5e26-8cfa-2245f93b43c5" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5983dd24-2080-5825-8480-5f2274507dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437488} {:answer/id #uuid "0e102cb8-95ed-551e-b324-574d91856376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e102cb8-95ed-551e-b324-574d91856376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437489} :answer-field/id #uuid "9976f639-ca02-5381-b2aa-6395e8fa240c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f651060-09a7-5bca-b60d-23499a5ade1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437490} {:answer/id #uuid "68311819-84c1-5ca2-838b-c9726a82aa3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f651060-09a7-5bca-b60d-23499a5ade1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437490} :answer-field/id #uuid "85ff90ba-f104-55c6-bf85-0b1d81813f2a" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1a3b9d0-0c1b-59de-a334-3a63ab59091a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437492} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea564e5-643b-50ad-aa53-8fc6a194153f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ea564e5-643b-50ad-aa53-8fc6a194153f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437493} :answer-field/id #uuid "6121fd51-e1aa-5684-9cb7-f09fc1d8d409" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56135889-753b-5df4-829a-e16e02adbe8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105692" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d0a06b24d18fac0e76a6d6f7cfc5409288c1b4dc7b1325d45b0ef30a8e3362f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has a curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/6c/6cb2333688e1a4a255398262d43046554c817705f09f7be9d6e6d082af519c42.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d78c56-0653-549d-8fe9-e600bbc18e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437510} {:answer/id #uuid "7fda3753-247c-5e38-a385-69d3789ea1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d78c56-0653-549d-8fe9-e600bbc18e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437510} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46aee06-be1c-589d-8527-7c703976fa69" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc92ea1-396a-5412-b8bd-1b4004d4228c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437512} {:answer/id #uuid "0568e3f2-60bd-5c83-9d49-f6bb4d6708c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0568e3f2-60bd-5c83-9d49-f6bb4d6708c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437513} :answer-field/id #uuid "13972053-f581-5ed1-b4ad-918c440107af" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f38ae9-f0f2-572d-9185-5d097fca9a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437514} {:answer/id #uuid "2db0b74d-25fc-5ea3-b717-639ac2457432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db0b74d-25fc-5ea3-b717-639ac2457432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437515} :answer-field/id #uuid "04460364-e8a3-51e8-83a3-921fcf6f1abf" :answer-field/key "$F$ is not irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78a7026b-7d30-5e52-a908-0666dbeb58d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437516} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7bb458-d9d7-5e5c-bb23-6322f015cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78a7026b-7d30-5e52-a908-0666dbeb58d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437516} :answer-field/id #uuid "472e5e59-acc9-5f2c-a05c-ad46e9a3685c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dbe3e81-bcac-55ba-b175-6059759ab5dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105695" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cc62b0a51519230bd1230874c00e17f165c345d11bc64e6d3c8fcf7788a5ee8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statements “$F$ is not irrotational” is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into from the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$F$ is not irrotational” only."}]}
